nly exists. But two of 798's five out-neighbours are the top-2 hubs in the entire graph \u2014 389 (625 events) and 1450 (593 events) (step_07, step_08). Static reachability through such hubs is essentially guaranteed for any node pair and is exactly the confounder the task warns against; it is not evidence of a cascade.\n- Decisive limitation: none of the available tools expose event timestamps or per-edge time ranges. I can establish static reachability and volume, but I cannot verify the two properties that define the claim \u2014 monotonically increasing times and consecutive gaps \u2264 600 within [4302, 42701]. With a 600-unit gap budget against a 38,399-unit window and a \u22653-hop requirement, the claim is neither confirmable nor refutable from the evidence I could obtain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d7716db7\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"798's out-neighbourhood {45,187,389,494,1450} and 131's in-neighbourhood {56,504,972,1637,1877,1932} are disjoint, so any cascade needs at least three hops. The 2-hop subgraphs of both nodes overlap, so a time-ignoring path exists, but it runs through 389 and 1450, the two most active nodes in the graph (625 and 593 events), which makes static reachability near-automatic and therefore uninformative. Both endpoints are themselves low-volume (8 and 14 events), so neither volume nor popularity supports a cascade either. Critically, no available tool exposes timestamps, so I could not test whether any candidate path is monotonically increasing in time with consecutive gaps <= 600 inside [4302, 42701]. The temporal evidence required for a 'present' or 'absent' verdict is simply not obtainable here, so I report insufficient.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 21335, "total_output_tokens": 4270, "total_tokens": 25605, "total_latency_ms": 62489, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}